					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-435303#post-1706991</guid>
				<title>explains the joke</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-435303/knee-deep-in-the-keter#post-1706991</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sun, 10 Feb 2013 00:08:54 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>thedeadlymoose</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>732274</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <ul> <li>This is for Project Crossover - with the video game &quot;Doom&quot;, in this case. The flying skulls and other demonic NPCs, as well as the Mars' moons setting, and the portal to Hell and fighting through Hell, are all from Doom.</li> <li>Able is like a video game PC or enemy; he can pull weapons out of nowhere (like most FPS characters), can take a ridiculous number of bullets to the face before dying, and respawns once killed. The joke here is that he <em>is</em> a video game PC.</li> <li>Doom involves a Portal To Hell, and Able is heavily implied to be &quot;Abel&quot; from Cain &amp; Abel, so half of this involves playing up Biblical references.</li> <li>Able has a pig farm because Abel in the Bible story raised animals.</li> <li>Guns lying around everywhere is also a Doom / general video game joke.</li> <li>The Serpent telling Able about Hell is again a reference to the early Genesis story.</li> <li>SCP-682 is the Devil, the Serpent, etc.</li> <li>&quot;I fucked your mom&quot; is a joke about extra-canonical implications &amp; mythos related to the Garden of Eden story, with the Serpent tempting Eve.</li> <li>&quot;Paul Bunyan's sequel&quot; refers to&#8230; you know what, fuck it, this is terrible, you can AT LEAST google THIS ONE. :P</li> </ul> <p>Why is it that our members who come off as <em>really</em> young are the ones who don't get this story? I really would not have expected that. Is it just coincidence? Or just me? Or what? I mean, shit, I never played Doom and this is still hilarious. :P</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
